WEBVTT

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:37.950
<b>June 21st, 2001 - West Indies</b>

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:43.620
<b>Guadalupe Base</b>

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:00.500
Princess Yui's tropical 
army uniform is pretty hot.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.520
Just seeing that alone made it worth coming.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.330
What are you even doing here?

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:06.520
Oh, come on.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:10.770
Half this test is just a game anyway.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:14.660
You're right about that.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.810
We'll be performing environmental endurance 
tests in a tropical environment,

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:26.070
and at the same time doing a photo shoot for 
media materials to raise wartime morale.

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:29.240
The Soviet Eishi will be helping us as well.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.950
The Scarlet Twins...

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:38.380
Ensign Manandal will be in charge of 
the Argos Flight side of the operation.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:40.690
Why me?

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.980
Media Command has decided that it 
would be best to show a united front

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:48.320
by having both parties involved in the 
accident the other day lead this operation.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:50.450
This is your chance to 
restore your reputation.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.820
So I'm supposed to clean 
up my own mess, is that it?

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.690
Everyone get ready.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:08.660
No matter the reason, this isn't 
a chance you get every day.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.370
Let's enjoy ourselves.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:14.010
The sun's too strong today.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:16.440
It's just so hot!

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:19.550
This isn't hot at all.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.950
Okay, Yuuya.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.820
We've got free time until this 
evening. You're coming with me.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:30.400
I'll show you how to enjoy 
your time at a resort.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:30.400
Hey,

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.390
wait!

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:36.440
<b>Ultramarine</b>

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.360
See, when you come to a resort,

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:51.030
you get to see a more liberated side of 
girls that you'd never be able to see otherwise.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.100
What are you talking about?

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:57.100
I'd imagine everybody's about ready to hit 
the showers and wash off all that sweat, right?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.040
So basically you're here to peek.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:03.990
What, you're not going?

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:07.540
Nope. It's not fair.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:09.620
Jeez, you're no fun.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.110
See you. I'm going.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.930
Maybe I should at least 
give them fair warning.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:27.750
It's Bridges.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.570
Tarisa, Stella, you here?

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:32.810
Something wrong?

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:36.580
Um... There's something I wanted to tell you.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.840
Sorry. I was in the shower.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.380
Um... well.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:44.800
What?

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.770
Um, I heard there's somebody suspicious 
around, so I wanted to let you know.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:51.720
B-Bye.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.070
Oh my.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.780
He's more of a kid than I thought.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:02.340
Test, test, test.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:07.590
Um, Argos Test Flight and Idar Test Flight.

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:11.500
I hope you'll spend time 
together and become close,

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.840
so that both test flights can be an 
example to the entire human race.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:16.800
Cheers!

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.220
Cheers!

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:27.770
Hey, VG.

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.270
What happened to your face?

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:30.200
Sunburn?

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.140
Yeah, something like that.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:36.700
I heard there was a suspicious 
person wandering around the base.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.810
What? This is a military base.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:43.540
But a squall came and 
they ran, it looks like.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.800
A really hot squall.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:48.000
A hot squall?

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:51.410
Come on, eat up, Yuuya.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.480
Y-Yeah.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:14.340
In a way, I attained my goal.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:22.550
But I badly wounded the 
hearts of the other Eishi.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:27.730
The Active Eagle isn't even 
made for close range combat...

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:34.560
If I'm letting this get to me, I'll 
be a failure as a development chief.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.260
Father...

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:46.360
What? I'm trying to be nice here.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:47.250
I don't need it.

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:51.070
I'm trying to be nice and 
you're just being a jerk!

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:55.920
I'm here because of orders. I won't eat meat.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:58.520
I'm not forcing you!

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.750
You're so quick to yell 
because your heart is weak.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:04.590
What was that?

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.700
You can threaten me but I'm not scared.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:07.870
Because you're weak.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.040
Why you...

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:12.680
Inia... is this some kind of trap?

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.350
What are you trying to do?

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.840
She gives me a bad feeling.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:19.330
Same to you!

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:24.710
I guess Russians can't understand 
other people's kindness.

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:27.370
How sad.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:31.350
Don't you ever want to get along 
with the people around you?

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.730
We're here because we've 
been ordered to come here.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:38.000
Nothing more and nothing less.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:38.940
Let's go, Inia.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:41.730
Hey, wait! We're not done here!

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:42.910
Stop it!

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.820
Did you forget what the Captain said?

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:50.190
We can't be friends with those guys!

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.280
Hell no.

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:55.320
Phoebe, get it!

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.070
Got it!

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.580
I got sand in my bathing suit...

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:03.430
Let's go!

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:03.950
Yeah!

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:07.840
I guess some people here had 
a lot of fun last night.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.130
If you're going to get into arguments,

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:13.270
you should have a competition 
to settle who's better instead.

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:14.840
What do you mean?

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:16.830
Ready, go!

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:21.090
Awesome.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:24.700
No!

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.840
I don't want to be away from Cryska!

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.350
This is an order too.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:33.760
No! I'm scared of the ocean.

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:37.310
Um, it's okay, Inia...

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:38.600
No!

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:40.530
Come on already.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:43.610
I can't believe I got stuck with her.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:47.840
I'm not going.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:50.320
Okay, I'll take her place.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:50.320
Fine, I'll go in her place.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.870
Alright, great!

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:57.750
Okay, you two enjoy your boat race!

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:58.350
What?

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:12.750
Damn, I wanted to play beach volleyball too.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:13.970
We don't have a choice.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:16.730
We decided by rock paper scissors.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.290
Hey, look at that.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:22.940
Doesn't something seem odd?

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:23.740
What?

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:26.110
Are they having some problem?

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:34.010
Damn it!

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.860
Hey, Yuuya!

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:40.610
You get back to the island and 
let them know what's going on.

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:41.930
I'll go see what's happening.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:47.710
Are you okay?

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:48.470
Hang in there.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:52.590
What's wrong?

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:54.300
Ensign Barchenowa.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:09:59.600
Lieutenant.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.550
Ensign Bridges.

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:03.180
Why are...

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.330
What happened?

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:07.320
Cryska?

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:11.220
She just collapsed.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:13.470
As soon as we got offshore 
she started getting pale...

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:17.600
I kept asking her but 
she said she was fine...

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:19.420
Some kind of seizure?

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:20.660
I don't know.

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:22.860
Anyway, we should turn back.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:25.110
I agree.

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:26.320
Give me an oar.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.550
Sorry about this. Thanks.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:38.920
I'll paddle from the front. You 
stay in the rear and watch Cryska.

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:40.910
Got it.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:47.840
Okay, let's...

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:58.140
We'll head to that island for now.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:10:59.260
Got it.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:10:59.930
Let's hurry.

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:13.760
We'll drag it straight up. Got it?

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.010
Let's go.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.870
3, 2, 1.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.650
Are you okay?

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:31.930
Yeah.

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:50.250
How does Cryska look?

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:55.550
I'd like to put something on her, but there 
wasn't an emergency blanket in that boat.

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:58.940
Don't military regs say you always 
have to have a first aid kit onboard?

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:03.560
Anyway, I'm worried about 
her losing body heat.

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:07.350
We need to get her out of 
this rain as fast as we can.

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:10.460
Got it. Let's move.

00:12:10.460 --> 00:12:12.000
Help me move her, Lt.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:12.760
Yeah.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:27.670
If we get up there it'll keep off the rain.

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:29.030
We're almost there.

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:30.080
Got it.

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:32.560
What's wrong?

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:33.530
Are you okay?

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:36.120
It's nothing.

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:38.000
Don't worry about it.

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.550
Are you sure you're okay?

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:43.860
Just a little tired.

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.690
Let's hurry. I'm worried about her.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.690
Yeah. Okay.

00:12:52.150 --> 00:12:52.710
Hey...

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:55.550
I'm sorry.

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.660
Did you hurt your leg? When?

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:08.580
Back there, when I slipped on the sand...

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:12.960
Are you okay?

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:14.870
Yeah.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:17.450
Back there?

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:18.780
Why didn't you say anything?

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:22.430
It wasn't that bad at first.

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:24.620
But as I kept walking...

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.600
Damn it. What do we do?

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:31.660
Can you go alone?

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:36.590
I know you're exhausted,

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.120
and I'm sorry to ask this.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:42.040
But take her yourself.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:44.030
But then you'll...

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:45.980
I'll catch up.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:49.050
We can't leave her like this.

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:50.500
Please.

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:56.930
Got it.

00:13:57.610 --> 00:13:58.760
Just wait.

00:13:58.760 --> 00:13:59.950
I'll be back soon.

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:01.090
No.

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:04.560
Your first priority needs to be 
to make a fire and warm her up.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:05.830
Got it?

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:10.560
I'll be back once I'm done with that.

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:11.640
Stay here and rest.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:12.560
Don't move from this spot.

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:14.570
Get going.

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:53.970
Pathetic.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:58.560
Staggering just from 
paddling a boat like that.

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.830
Do I have a fever?

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.700
It's so strange how the rain feels good...

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:22.070
Takamura-san...

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:25.710
Please.

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:27.770
Save me.

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.220
Save me. Hurry.

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.020
Please!

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.540
Why?

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.400
A dream?

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:57.780
What am I doing? I'm barely even hurt.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:15:58.850
I...

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:14.770
Don't force yourself!

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:19.880
I'm sorry for making you wait.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:25.120
What are you doing?

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:26.610
What happened with Ensign Barchenowa?

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:27.630
Don't worry about her.

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:28.880
Of course I'm worried about her.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:34.080
It's all swelled up.

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.540
I told you not to try to move.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:39.140
It doesn't matter.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:43.820
More importantly, why did you leave 
someone alone when they're unconscious?

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.300
I don't have time to explain.

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:48.170
Get back to her.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:49.740
I'll get there myself.

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:51.070
Knock it off.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:53.320
You can barely move.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:06.580
You're always willing to put yourself 
second and the mission first, right?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:08.920
What are you trying to say?

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:12.080
I'm already here.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:17.030
If you really want to make me head 
back to Cryska as fast as possible,

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:20.080
isn't the best thing to do to stop arguing?

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:26.150
Or what? Are all those lectures 
you gave me just crap,

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.980
and your pride is the only 
thing that matters to you?

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:33.540
Fine.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:34.750
Help me walk.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:35.970
You're kidding.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:37.860
Did you say something?

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.260
No. Nothing.

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:42.880
Okay, let's go.

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:45.840
It'd be faster to carry you.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:50.100
Fine then.

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:53.610
Stay put.

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:03.280
Wait! Wait a second.

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:05.440
Would you shut up for a second?

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:07.450
To be honest, I'm dead tired.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:17.030
Right. If you want to get this 
over with, then help me out.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:19.340
I'm sorry, Ensign.

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:21.030
You're right.

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:23.250
Is this better?

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:26.780
T-Thanks.

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:29.940
It makes it a lot easier.

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:31.720
I'm sorry about this.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:44.060
She seems stable,

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:48.680
but since we don't know the 
cause, there's reason to worry.

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:56.840
This island is probably only a few minutes 
away from the bases by helicopter or TSF.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:59.560
It shouldn't take them that long to find us.

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:07.590
Ensign.

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:10.360
Can I ask something?

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:12.250
What is it?

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:17.320
Well... I don't want to intrude 
into your private life.

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:20.370
But what's your relationship to her?

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:22.410
What do you mean?

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:24.220
Um, nothing special.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:29.480
But it struck me as odd the way you 
referred to her by her first name.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.750
And there's nothing special 
about that either.

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:39.600
When I was captured in the Soviet base, 
the other Eishi with her called her that.

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:48.690
So I just called her Cryska without thinking.

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.140
I see.

00:19:55.070 --> 00:20:00.370
The other Eishi, who was with 
you when you were captured...

00:20:00.370 --> 00:20:01.620
Inia?

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:04.100
It's strange you'd be bothered by that.

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:11.800
I see. You suspect me of something.

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:14.570
That I'm leaking information 
to the Soviets...

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:15.910
No!

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:18.060
Nobody suspects you of anything.

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:20.990
That's not it. Not at all.

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:22.210
Just...

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:23.690
Just what?

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:28.430
Come on.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:31.000
I'm sorry. Forget it.

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:33.640
I shouldn't have asked.

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:37.680
Seriously? You can't just 
leave me hanging like that.

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:43.480
Christ.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.410
Wait, Ensign.

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:46.530
Where are you going?

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:48.260
The rain's slowed down.

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:49.350
I'm going to check out the boat.

00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:51.530
O-Okay.

00:20:56.340 --> 00:21:01.480
Honestly... it was stupid of 
me to ask about Ensign Sestina.

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:03.650
Inia...

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:06.340
Ensign Barchenowa?

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:08.290
Where am I?

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:10.770
Are you okay? How do you feel?

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:18.610
I see. I guess I'm in your debt.

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:20.000
Don't worry about it.

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:23.060
The bad weather isn't your fault.

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:25.750
So where's Ensign Bridges?

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:27.320
He went to check on the boat.

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:29.450
He'll be back shortly.

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:30.510
I see.

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:35.800
Lt. Takamura.

00:21:36.840 --> 00:21:38.120
What?

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:40.100
Can I ask you something?

00:21:40.870 --> 00:21:41.720
Yeah.

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:46.520
It might not be the best time to ask, but...

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:51.110
It's a very private question.

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:52.320
Private?

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:58.330
Don't worry, it's nothing classified.

00:21:58.770 --> 00:21:59.810
I see.

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:01.970
Very well.

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:03.830
What do you want to ask?

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:07.330
I'd like you to tell me about Yuuya Bridges.

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:11.400
He interests me.

00:22:28.370 --> 00:22:30.260
It throws me off.

00:22:30.260 --> 00:22:31.890
Act like you always do, damn it.

00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:40.250
If you want to say something, 
say it. Like you always do.

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:50.680
You're kidding me!

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:53.240
The boat...

00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:09.250
The mood here is awful.

00:24:09.250 --> 00:24:10.800
Give me a break.

00:24:11.320 --> 00:24:13.140
This has never happened before.

00:24:13.140 --> 00:24:15.700
It all started when he came!

00:24:15.700 --> 00:24:18.650
Just get out! Don't look!

00:24:16.970 --> 00:24:24.270
<b>Wanderer's Whereabouts</b>

00:24:19.510 --> 00:24:22.090
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.090 --> 00:24:23.860
Wanderer's Whereabouts.
